From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray 3D: open the next clip's second view ahead of the join

The base view's next play item is read ahead of the join, so a share
that stops answering near a join is seen as a source running dry and
the player buffers. The second view's file of the next play item was
still opened, probed and sought at the join, on the player thread, and
its demuxer found the play item's start by searching the file by
timestamp, a read at a score of places. In an outage each of those
blocked for as long as the share was gone: the player declared a still
frame, the clock ran on, and playback jumped ahead by the length of the
outage once the share answered.

The second view of the next play item is now opened, probed and sought
by the clip reader with the base view's next file, on the same thread of
its own, from what is taken from libbluray on the player thread before.
The reader opens it at the join too when it was not prepared, so the
input stream only takes it.
The join waits for both, and takes the second view if it is the one
asked for; the current play item's is kept until its join, which comes
after the base view's. Its demuxer seeks by the entry points of the
clip's .clpi, a single seek that a play item's start, read ahead,
already holds; the .clpi is read once per clip. Abort ends a stalled
open or probe, ahead or at the join. A playlist change drops what was
prepared ahead, and a disc opened as a disc, without the clip reader,
opens the second view at the join as before. The second view's cache is
throttled to the title's rate as the base view's clips are.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
